{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Coverage check on the verification finding, done by reading the two captured tests that exercise VerifyLeader. TestRaft_VerifyLeader_PartialConnect uses a three-voter cluster with one follower disconnected and expects success, because a voter quorum of two remains reachable; TestRaft_VerifyLeader_Fail forces a follower to a higher term so the leader steps down and expects ErrNotLeader or ErrLeadershipLost. Neither test introduces a non-voter, so the captured suite neither contradicts nor covers the acknowledgement path this finding rests on. The account gains that as counterevidence with the test lines as a source; no execution or conclusion changes.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-verifyleader-tests\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft_test.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2099,\\\"end_line\\\":2172,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"f6dbda4bb1ee4baca7e8f055f109412f-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"s-lease\\\",\\\"s-quorum\\\",\\\"s-verifyleader-doc\\\",\\\"s-verifyleader-tests\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"7401ab5a8f7c4cd69d947e972ea31a61\\\":[22,23,24,25,26,27],\\\"c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862\\\":[22,23,24,25],\\\"5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9\\\":[22,23]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Three receipts answer this question. The first (5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9 at indices 22 and 23) measured the isolation with slowed timers; the second (c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862 at 22-25) ran it with slowed and default timers; the third (7401ab5a8f7c4cd69d947e972ea31a61 at 22-27) repeats both cases and measures when the isolated leader stops reporting itself as leader.\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: leader verification can be satisfied without a voter quorum, and the resulting incorrect answer is available for about one lease interval before the same node stops leading. Evidence: in the latest receipt the slowed-timer setup event 22 records three voters with a quorum of two, a voter unreachable by direct AppendEntries and a reachable non-voter, and its result event 23 records verification succeeding with no error in under a millisecond while the node still led; events 25 and 26 repeat the premise and the same result with the repository's default in-memory timers; the bound events 24 and 27 record the node becoming a follower after 1012 ms with a 1000 ms lease and after 60 ms with the default 50 ms lease. Mechanism from source: verifyLeader starts its count at one for itself and registers the future in every entry of the leader's replication map, which startStopReplication builds for every server of the configuration except the leader without filtering by suffrage; each peer's heartbeat acknowledges the pending verification on a successful AppendEntries, so a non-voter's acknowledgement raises the count to the voter quorum computed from voters alone, while the lease check counts voters only and therefore closes the window about one lease interval later. The documented purpose of the call, anchored, is to ensure the peer is still the leader and to prevent returning stale data from the FSM after leadership is lost, which is what a non-voter acknowledgement cannot establish. Coverage: the captured tests that exercise this call use voter-only clusters, so nothing in the snapshot pins the non-voter path either way.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The measured bound limits the impact: the node stops reporting itself as leader about one lease interval after losing the voter quorum, so the incorrect verification result is available only inside that interval.\\\",\n    \\\"The defect requires a configuration containing non-voters; in a voters-only cluster every replication peer is a voter and the acknowledgement set equals the voter set, so the path cannot diverge from the voter quorum. The captured verification tests are exactly that shape: a three-voter cluster with one follower disconnected expects success because a voter quorum remains reachable, and a forced higher term on a follower expects ErrNotLeader or ErrLeadershipLost.\\\",\n    \\\"No write path is affected: entry commitment uses the commitment map, which contains voters only, so this is a read-verification path rather than a commit-rule path.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe calls VerifyLeader directly rather than through an application that then serves a read, so the stale-read consequence is argued from the anchored documentation rather than measured end to end.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on four-peer in-memory clusters with the repository's own facilities; production timings and transports are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The bound is reported for the two timer configurations used (1000 ms and the default 50 ms lease) and depends on the lease timeout, not on a fixed wall-clock constant.\\\",\n    \\\"Both cases isolate the leader by transport disconnection and confirm it with direct AppendEntries attempts recorded in the same events.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
